    {
      "id": "5ObKU3LXbzhW7QUP7oEsL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1848.3895412978554,
      "y": 4112.862658723313,
      "width": 1208.4728532181944,
      "height": 350.0398173310536,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 106487175,
      "version": 1153,
      "versionNonce": 724354663,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786714483634,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Closing Thoughts on this Draft:\n\nI looked at the ST source code and there if we start reading from the\n`drawregion` function, it calls `xdrawline` for the dirty lines and that calls two interesting functions\n`xmakeglyphfontspecs` and `xdrawglyphfontspecs`, the first one goes over all the codepoints &\nreturns us a GlyphFontSpec array which is equivalent to the GlyphInfo, just with the font attached for each Glyph..\n\n\nThen the draw counterpart draws hcunks at a time somehow (didn't look into the details, though seems not\nthat complicated) => one pass for the background, one for the foreground and draws symbols with the same\nforeground/background/mode together.",
      "fontSize": 23.57170487077802,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Closing Thoughts on this Draft:\n\nI looked at the ST source code and there if we start reading from the\n`drawregion` function, it calls `xdrawline` for the dirty lines and that calls two interesting functions\n`xmakeglyphfontspecs` and `xdrawglyphfontspecs`, the first one goes over all the codepoints &\nreturns us a GlyphFontSpec array which is equivalent to the GlyphInfo, just with the font attached for each Glyph..\n\n\nThen the draw counterpart draws hcunks at a time somehow (didn't look into the details, though seems not\nthat complicated) => one pass for the background, one for the foreground and draws symbols with the same\nforeground/background/mode together.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
